<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>HaulTimes</title><link>https://haultimes.com/</link><description>Freight and trucking news for the US and Canada</description><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:41:42 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Mexico&#x27;s Border Freight Needs Smarter Truck Scheduling</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/mexico-s-border-freight-needs-smarter-truck-scheduling-d07c5e25ad/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/mexico-s-border-freight-needs-smarter-truck-scheduling-d07c5e25ad/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:25:10 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>Mexico Business News</description></item><item><title>Three supply chain trends carriers should watch heading into 2027</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/three-supply-chain-trends-carriers-should-watch-heading-into-2027-c7e69a5d82/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/three-supply-chain-trends-carriers-should-watch-heading-into-2027-c7e69a5d82/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:08:48 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>In a FleetOwner column, the chief executive of a Lincoln, Nebraska freight brokerage outlines three supply chain trends he expects fleet owners to watch in 2027. He cites Bureau of Labor Statistics data showing that trucking has lost more than 100,000 jobs since 2023, although the decline slowed in 2026. Using mileage and fuel-economy figures from the American Transportation Research Institute and Department of Energy diesel prices from early 2026 onward, he estimates that higher diesel costs add roughly $40,000 a year per truck, or $400,000 for a 10-truck fleet. He warns that if a recession pushed rates below operating costs, some carriers would be forced to haul freight at a loss. He also argues that driver shortages will keep pressure on pay, which fuel costs make harder to fund.</description></item><item><title>Aetherion receives $2 million for Volvo CNG truck trials in Canada</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/aetherion-receives-2-million-for-volvo-cng-truck-trials-in-canada-2308c68700/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/aetherion-receives-2-million-for-volvo-cng-truck-trials-in-canada-2308c68700/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:35:21 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Could microrefineries help lower diesel prices in northern Canada?</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/could-microrefineries-help-lower-diesel-prices-in-northern-canada-1b3bc19f28/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/could-microrefineries-help-lower-diesel-prices-in-northern-canada-1b3bc19f28/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:07:43 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>CBC</description></item><item><title>Einride Says Contracted Revenue Grew 76% to $167 Million</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/einride-says-contracted-revenue-grew-76-to-167-million-64bdaec7ec/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/einride-says-contracted-revenue-grew-76-to-167-million-64bdaec7ec/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:02:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Einride, the Swedish autonomous and electric freight company listed on Nasdaq as ENRD, said its contracted annual recurring revenue was about $167 million as of November 2026, up 76% from $95 million at the end of June. In a third-quarter business update issued November 18, 2026, it reported constant currency revenue of SEK 185.9 million ($18.3 million), a 27% rise from the second quarter. The company said it has added eight customers since June, bringing its total to more than 40. Its two cab-less electric trucks for EASE Logistics went into daily freight operations in Marysville, Ohio, in September. The company reaffirmed second-half 2026 revenue guidance of $39-42 million, but its adjusted EBITDA outlook for that period was widened to negative $39 to 41 million.</description></item><item><title>FMCSA Motus Backlog Swells: 25,000+ Pending Applications Stalled Without Insurance</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-motus-backlog-swells-25-000-pending-applications-stalled-without-5254d6f2cd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fmcsa-motus-backlog-swells-25-000-pending-applications-stalled-without-5254d6f2cd/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:06:59 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Paramvir Singh Gets 30 Months in $7.2M Cargo Theft Case</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/paramvir-singh-gets-30-months-in-7-2m-cargo-theft-case-84be4694d7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/paramvir-singh-gets-30-months-in-7-2m-cargo-theft-case-84be4694d7/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:15:11 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>edhat</description></item><item><title>Strongsville Costco shooting victim’s family sues trucking companies, claims they ignored warning signs</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/strongsville-costco-shooting-victim-s-family-sues-trucking-companies-c-2ab81688b4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/strongsville-costco-shooting-victim-s-family-sues-trucking-companies-c-2ab81688b4/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:56:02 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>News 5 Cleveland WEWS</description></item><item><title>A Cincinnati suburb erupts over trucks, mosque and Uzbeks</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/a-cincinnati-suburb-erupts-over-trucks-mosque-and-uzbeks-5974bfaec0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/a-cincinnati-suburb-erupts-over-trucks-mosque-and-uzbeks-5974bfaec0/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Cincinnati Enquirer</description><